    <completion>Verified inline by the orchestrator (2026-07-29) via grep + code-review. FR-17 PASS: every `surfaceLaunchRegistry` reference in record-driven paths (`ribbon/AnalysisRecordLaunch.ts`, `workspace/WorkspacePane.tsx` analysis-entry) is an explanatory COMMENT asserting record-driven opens go via `openSpaarkeAi`, NOT the registry. The only actual `surfaceLaunchRegistry` USAGE is in `conversation/ConversationPane.tsx` — the reactive in-chat/TEXT-path (deliberately OUT of scope; UQ-4=NO, no `workspace-tab` registry entry added). No record-driven ribbon/subgrid/deep-link path routes through the surface-launch registry. ADR-039 / §13.3 satisfied. Confirmed by task 052's own adr-check (0 violations) + the 041/050/052 launch chain being deep-link only.</completion>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>ADR-039 compliance verification over the entry surface authored in 050/052 — grep + code-review confirmation, no new implementation surface; not a build/architecture change.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Bounded verification/enforcement task (grep + review against a single ADR rule); no design judgment required beyond the documented UQ-4 = NO decision.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>medium</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
