  <prompt>
    Enforce ADR-039 / §13.3 (FR-17): every record-driven open (ribbon + subgrid, cases 2b/2d) routes through the
    `openSpaarkeAi` deep-link, NOT `surfaceLaunchRegistry` — the registry is the reactive in-chat path (agent offers a
    surface), explicitly distinct from record-driven opens. Confirm by code review + grep that no record-driven path
    touches `surfaceLaunchRegistry`. Per UQ-4 = NO (owner 2026-07-28), the in-chat Assistant *offer* to open Agreement
    Analysis is OUT OF SCOPE — do NOT add a `workspace-tab` registry entry.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the Assistant surface-launch mechanism (ADR-039), the distinction between the
    record-driven `openSpaarkeAi` deep-link path and the reactive in-chat `surfaceLaunchRegistry` path. Follow ADRs strictly.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Verified evidence (code review + grep) that all record-driven opens (Matter/Project ribbon, record subgrid, entry cases
    2b/2d) route via `openSpaarkeAi`, and NO record-driven path routes through `surfaceLaunchRegistry`; no new `workspace-tab`
    registry entry is added (UQ-4 = NO); findings recorded in project notes.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      §13.3 / ADR-039: record-driven opens stay in CODE via `openSpaarkeAi`; `surfaceLaunchRegistry` is the reactive in-chat
      path (the Assistant offering a surface) and is explicitly distinct. UQ-4 (RESOLVED 2026-07-28) = NO for this project:
      the in-chat *offer* to open Agreement Analysis is a deferred later enhancement (deferring avoids chip mis-fire risk
      while the deterministic entry model is established). This task is the enforcement/verification gate over the entry
